    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option D (\"Bring food to share\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Invitation amicale):\nIn response to \"What does the host ask guests to do?\", the passage states: \"PRIVATE INVITATION — Dear friends, to celebrate moving into my new apartment, I invite you to a friendly picnic this Sunday starting at 12:00 PM at Laurentides Park. To vary the meal, everyone is asked to bring a salad or a dessert to share with the group!\".\nOption D (\"Bring food to share\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Give housewarming gifts\") [INCORRECT - LEXICAL LURE & UNSTATED ASSUMPTION]: Reuses passage keywords (\"Give housewarming gifts\") while introducing an unfounded deduction not present in the text.\n  - Option B (\"Contribute to reservation costs\") [INCORRECT - FACTUAL CONTRADICTION]: Asserts a condition (\"Contribute to reservation costs\") that directly contradicts the instructions or facts stated in the document.\n  - Option C (\"Arrive only after 3:00 PM\") [INCORRECT - NUMERICAL OR TEMPORAL DISTRACTOR TRAP]: Uses inaccurate numerical or temporal anchors (\"Arrive only after 3:00 PM\") that distort explicit passage figures.\n  - Option D (\"Bring food to share\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the verified information from the document without distortion."
