    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option B (\"Walking at least 30 minutes daily and taking stairs\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Avis de prévention médicale):\nIn response to \"What simple daily habit do health professionals recommend?\", the passage states: \"PUBLIC HEALTH — MUNICIPAL PREVENTION CAMPAIGN: IMPORTANCE OF DAILY PHYSICAL ACTIVITY.\n\nAddressing sedentary desk jobs, health authorities recommend at least 30 minutes of brisk daily walking. Simple habit changes, like taking stairs instead of elevators, help prevent chronic conditions.\n\nMunicipalities support this by installing outdoor fitness trails and free exercise equipment in public parks.\".\nOption B (\"Walking at least 30 minutes daily and taking stairs\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Mandatory sign-up at professional sports gyms\") [INCORRECT - EXTREME OVERSTATEMENT TRAP]: Presents an excessive or categorical judgment (\"Mandatory sign-up at professional sports gyms\") ignoring the article's balanced and nuanced synthesis.\n  - Option B (\"Walking at least 30 minutes daily and taking stairs\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the verified information from the document without distortion.\n  - Option C (\"Intensive two-hour running workouts every evening\") [INCORRECT - PERIPHERAL DETAIL DISTRACTOR]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Intensive two-hour running workouts every evening\") rather than the overarching conclusion of the observers.\n  - Option D (\"Buying expensive home weightlifting machinery\") [INCORRECT - OVERGENERALIZATION & CONTRADICTION]: Distorts reported experience by asserting (\"Buying expensive home weightlifting machinery\"), contradicting the general synthesis."
