    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option A (\"Using practical roleplay simulations of daily life situations\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Article sur l'alphabétisation):\nIn response to \"Preferred teaching method used during these French integration language classes:\", the passage states: \"SOCIAL INCLUSION — CIVIC LEARNING BULLETIN: FRENCH INTEGRATION LANGUAGE WORKSHOPS.\n\nFacilitating socio-professional integration for newcomers, non-profits offer evening French language classes. Through practical roleplay (grocery shopping, public transit, administrative forms), learners gain everyday linguistic independence.\n\nMastering French represents the key driver for social empowerment and accessing qualified employment opportunities.\".\nOption A (\"Using practical roleplay simulations of daily life situations\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Using practical roleplay simulations of daily life situations\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the verified information from the document without distortion.\n  - Option B (\"Rote memorization of complex academic grammar rules\") [INCORRECT - EXTREME OVERSTATEMENT TRAP]: Presents an excessive or categorical judgment (\"Rote memorization of complex academic grammar rules\") ignoring the article's balanced and nuanced synthesis.\n  - Option C (\"Strict prohibitions banning talking during class sessions\") [INCORRECT - PERIPHERAL DETAIL DISTRACTOR]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Strict prohibitions banning talking during class sessions\") rather than the overarching conclusion of the observers.\n  - Option D (\"Written translation of 17th-century literary classic novels\") [INCORRECT - OVERGENERALIZATION & CONTRADICTION]: Distorts reported experience by asserting (\"Written translation of 17th-century literary classic novels\"), contradicting the general synthesis."
