    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option A (\"Fixing broken items for free with volunteer assistance\")\n\n• Textual Evidence (Article sur la réparation collaborative):\nIn response to \"Core operational principle of neighborhood community Repair Cafes:\", the passage states: \"PRACTICAL LIFE — REPAIR-TOGETHER BULLETIN: RISING POPULARITY OF NEIGHBORHOOD REPAIR CAFES.\n\nFighting waste and planned obsolescence, volunteer mechanics and electricians host monthly 'Repair Café' events. Residents bring broken home appliances, torn clothing, or faulty bikes to fix them together for free over coffee.\n\nThis community initiative avoids new gear purchases while teaching practical DIY troubleshooting skills to visitors.\".\nOption A (\"Fixing broken items for free with volunteer assistance\") accurately conveys the essential information presented in the text.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Fixing broken items for free with volunteer assistance\") [CORRECT]: Accurately conveys the verified information from the document without distortion.\n  - Option B (\"Purchasing brand-new home appliances under retail warranty\") [INCORRECT - EXTREME OVERSTATEMENT TRAP]: Presents an excessive or categorical judgment (\"Purchasing brand-new home appliances under retail warranty\") ignoring the article's balanced and nuanced synthesis.\n  - Option C (\"Discarding all faulty items into special waste containers\") [INCORRECT - PERIPHERAL DETAIL DISTRACTOR]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Discarding all faulty items into special waste containers\") rather than the overarching conclusion of the observers.\n  - Option D (\"Paying expensive rates to commercial repair technicians\") [INCORRECT - OVERGENERALIZATION & CONTRADICTION]: Distorts reported experience by asserting (\"Paying expensive rates to commercial repair technicians\"), contradicting the general synthesis."
